  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Clinique Vétérinaire Univet Cannes Carnot, at 82-84 boulevard Carnot, is part of the Univet network and has a full technical platform: analysis lab, ultrasound, digital X-ray, scanner and a hospitalisation service with a separate kennel area. A solid address for your dog if you're staying around Cannes.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Consultations run Monday to Saturday, from 9am to 12pm and 2pm to 7pm. The Univet network's website also advertises an emergency service available 24/7 outside these hours; vet directories that repeat this information in fact merely copy this same original claim, and so do not amount to an independent confirmation. Targeted search for any negative signals (emergencies not actually handled, phone unreachable at night): none found. One negative review exists but concerns an entirely different matter (unpleasant reception, refusal to hand out medication without a new consultation) — comparable to the V2U Toulon case, it doesn't call the emergency service itself into question.</p>
      <div class="callout"><svg><use href="#i-alert"/></svg> Emergencies: the Univet network advertises a 24/7 emergency service for this clinic — a self-declared claim we were unable to confirm independently. Call the number shown to check what to do outside consultation hours.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Boulevard Carnot is in central Cannes, a few minutes' walk from the train station and the town centre.</p>
